1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:07,200
10 hundred thousands is called one million.

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:13,880
Written as 1 000 000.

3
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:27,020
10 million is called ten million. Written as 10 000 000.

4
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:44,600
10 ten millions is called hundred million. Written as 100 000 000.

5
00:00:45,420 --> 00:01:03,910
Millions class has three places: millions, ten millions, hundred millions.

6
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:13,420
See how to fill example at first line in table to perform second line.

7
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:24,770
Say: Number 53218762

8
00:01:24,770 --> 00:01:39,240
Read as: Fifty-three million, two hundred eighteen thousand, seven hundred sixty-two.

9
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:52,370
Number 53218762 consists of 8 digits

10
00:01:52,370 --> 00:02:05,150
Value of each digit depends on its position in number writing

11
00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:12,860
Digit 5 has value fifty million.

12
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:25,170
Digit 1 has value ten thousand.

13
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:34,080
Continue reading

14
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:42,970
Read number from millions class, thousands class then ones class.

15
00:02:42,970 --> 00:02:53,620
Number above is read: Three hundred twenty-five million, one hundred sixty-seven thousand, two hundred fifteen.

